Injection points for the port's tests, under the names of three of Apache
Cloudberry's faults inside PostgreSQL's own scan, recovery and promotion,
which query_conflict and faults in its hot-standby schedule of isolation2
set on a mirror: a scan of a heap page held once the page's lock is let go
and its pin still held, in the table the test names, so that the replay of
a VACUUM of the page waits for the pin; the startup process having
signalled the backends that may hold the pin it waits for, which the test
waits for before it lets the scan go; and a promotion come as far as the
node no longer being in recovery, which a test waits for after FTS has
promoted a mirror:

  heapgetpage_after_unlock_buffer          heapam.c, heap_prepare_pagescan()
  recovery_conflict_bufferpin_signal_sent  standby.c, SendRecoveryConflictWithBufferPin()
  out_of_recovery_in_startupxlog           xlog.c, StartupXLOG()

gp_core's fault injector attaches a fault of Cloudberry's name to the point
(gp_fault.c), the first with the table's name, as heap_insert's.  They serve
tests alone, so they are not in the core series: Dockerfile.pg applies this
after test-iso2-recovery.patch, to the tree of either ref, vanilla or
patched, so that the two images still differ only in the ref.  Dormant, as
any point is: without injection points the macro is empty, and with them a
point nothing attached to runs no callback.


--- a/src/backend/access/heap/heapam.c
+++ b/src/backend/access/heap/heapam.c
@@ -699,6 +699,16 @@
 	}
 
 	LockBuffer(buffer, BUFFER_LOCK_UNLOCK);
+
+	/*
+	 * A test may hold a scan here, the page's lock let go and its pin held,
+	 * the point's callback given the table's name.
+	 */
+	{
+		const char *names[2] = {"", RelationGetRelationName(scan->rs_base.rs_rd)};
+
+		INJECTION_POINT("heapgetpage_after_unlock_buffer", (void *) names);
+	}
 }
 
 /*
--- a/src/backend/access/transam/xlog.c
+++ b/src/backend/access/transam/xlog.c
@@ -6189,6 +6189,9 @@
 	 */
 	InRecovery = false;
 
+	/* A test may wait for a promotion to have come this far, here. */
+	INJECTION_POINT("out_of_recovery_in_startupxlog", NULL);
+
 	/* start the archive_timeout timer and LSN running */
 	XLogCtl->lastSegSwitchTime = (pg_time_t) time(NULL);
 	XLogCtl->lastSegSwitchLSN = EndOfLog;
--- a/src/backend/storage/ipc/standby.c
+++ b/src/backend/storage/ipc/standby.c
@@ -888,6 +888,9 @@
 	 * own fate.
 	 */
 	SignalRecoveryConflictWithDatabase(InvalidOid, reason);
+
+	/* A test may wait until the backends have been signalled, here. */
+	INJECTION_POINT("recovery_conflict_bufferpin_signal_sent", NULL);
 }
 
